@startuml seq-protected-request
' =====================================================================
'  SEQUENCE — protected request + PERM_* authorization (defence in depth)
' =====================================================================
title Sequence — Protected request (PERM_* authorization)

skinparam shadowing false
actor "User (SPA)" as U
participant "gateway-service\n:9000" as GW
participant "Keycloak JWK\n:8081" as JWK
participant "downstream service\n(e.g. roaming :9002)" as SVC

U -> GW : GET /api/roaming/anomalies\nAuthorization: Bearer <JWT>
GW -> JWK : fetch/validate signature (JWK set, cached)
JWK --> GW : keys
GW -> GW : extract claims →\nROLE_* (realm_access) + PERM_* (platform-client)

alt has PERM_roaming-events:read
  GW -> SVC : forward (still bearing JWT) lb://roaming-analysis-service
  SVC -> SVC : re-validate JWT + @PreAuthorize(PERM_roaming-events:read)
  SVC --> GW : 200 payload
  GW --> U : 200 payload
else missing permission
  GW --> U : 403 Forbidden
else missing / expired token
  GW --> U : 401 Unauthorized
end

note over GW, SVC
  Authorize on the PERMISSION, never the role name (ADR-07).
  Enforced at the gateway AND again in the service → defence in depth.
  A public path must be permitted at BOTH tiers or the gateway 401s first.
end note

@enduml
